MBP packed SIMD in Rocket's ALU, per tile

Four R-type instructions in custom-0 (opcode 0x0B), funct7 = 0, integrated into
Rocket's ALU as single-cycle two-read ops and enabled per tile by a new
RocketCoreParams field:

    funct3 0  MBP.DOT8   rd = sum_{i=0..7} sext(rs1.b[i]) * sext(rs2.b[i])
    funct3 1  MBP.MAX8   rd.b[i] = max_signed(rs1.b[i], rs2.b[i])
    funct3 2  MBP.QMUL   rd = (sext32(rs1) * sext32(rs2) + 2^30) >> 31, round-half-up
    funct3 3  MBP.CLIP8  rd = sext64(clamp(rs1, -128, +127)), rs2 ignored

The contract and the bit-exact C reference are fpga/pynq-z2/sw/pext.h; the
specification, the workload evidence and the DECISION block that split the fused
requantize into QMUL + a scalar shift + CLIP8 are fpga/pynq-z2/docs/PEXT_SPEC.md;
the measured cost menu is fpga/pynq-z2/docs/PEXT_FEASIBILITY.md.

FOUR FILES, AND WHY EACH:

  tile/Core.scala        usePExt on the CoreParams trait, as a CONCRETE def with a
                         false default -- NOT an abstract val like useZba/useZbb/
                         useZbs beside it -- so that every other core implementing
                         CoreParams (BOOM, Shuttle, the groundtest and tracegen
                         tiles) needs no change at all.

  rocket/RocketCore.scala  the RocketCoreParams field that overrides it, the
                         PExtDecode entry in decode_table, and a require() that
                         refuses to elaborate usePExt together with RoCC, because
                         RoCCDecode claims ALL of custom-0 and reads funct3 as a
                         register-usage code -- the two tables would hand
                         DecodeLogic contradictory outputs for one instruction.

  rocket/IDecode.scala   the four BitPats and the PExtDecode table. DW_XPR, not
                         DW_32: the ALU sign-extends its result from bit 31 when
                         dw is DW_32, which would silently break DOT8's range and
                         QMUL's top bit.

  rocket/ALU.scala       fn codes 20-23 (the only free codes in the 5-bit space
                         besides 27) and the datapath, adapted from the measured
                         out-of-context modules in fpga/pynq-z2/rtl_study/pext/.

HART 1 MUST TRAP. Without usePExt a tile gets no PExtDecode table and no datapath,
so custom-0 decodes as illegal and raises an illegal-instruction exception. That is
the heterogeneity mechanism (PEXT_SPEC.md 7.6), not a degradation path, and
samples/pext_rtl_selftest checks that the trap HAPPENS, with mcause == 2, mepc at
the instruction, and rd unwritten.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES TO A CONFIG THAT DOES NOT SET usePExt: nothing. Elaborating
PynqZ2RocketBigLittleTacitConfig before and after leaves 500 of 505 generated
files byte-identical; the five that differ carry only firtool source-locator
comments whose line numbers moved, plus one simulation-only $error string inside
an `ifndef SYNTHESIS` block that quotes an assertion's own source line
("RocketCore.scala:910" -> "RocketCore.scala:926"). Stripped of comments, all five
are identical. Verified, not asserted -- scripts/09_patch_rocket_pext.sh --verify
reproduces it.

